  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive isotope having a half - life period of $3$ days was received after $12$ days. If $3 \\mathrm{~g}$ of the isotope is left in the container, what would be the initial mass of the isotope ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZsIVt",
      "text": "\n$12 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bzwUI",
      "text": "\n$36 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DpLuG",
      "text": "\n$48 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EPD3w",
      "text": "\n$24 \\mathrm{~g}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $t_{1 / 2}=3$\nTotal time $\\mathrm{T}=12$\nNo. of half lives $(n)=\\frac{12}{3}=4$\n$\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n=\\frac{\\mathrm{N}}{\\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{o}}}$\n$\\therefore \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^4=\\frac{3}{\\mathrm{~N}_{\\mathrm{o}}}$\n$\\frac{3}{\\mathrm{~N}_{\\mathrm{o}}}=\\frac{1}{16}$\n$\\mathrm{~N}_{\\mathrm{o}}=48 \\mathrm{~g}$",
    "image": null
  },
